$Id: README.internals,v 1.5 2011/12/23 23:34:31 drmiller Exp $

Communication between the Front End and the simulator is via two pipes,
one for each direction. All communication is in units of uint16_t.

The simulator reads and interprets the following (binary) codes on
it's input pipe:

00000000kkkkkkkk
	Keyboard code 'k' was entered. E.g. the user presses "Search" and
	the code 0x0080 is sent to the simulator on the pipe.

0000000100000kkk
	"Special" key: PRIME, SET P.C., VERIFY PROG, RECORD PROG, and SHIFT
	variations. 'k' is the microcode address to jump to:
	0 = RESET
	1 = REWIND
	2 = FORWARD
	3 = (STOP ?)
	4 = (APR ?)
	5 = n/a
	6 = n/a
	7 = n/a

000000100000mmmm
	Mode register 0 changed, new value is 'mm'.
	Bit meanings, 1/(0):
	b0 = RIGHT
	b1 = DOUBLE
	b2 = RECORD
	b3 = TRANS.
	RECORD & TRANS. = "EDIT" (PLAY and RECORD down)

000000110000mmmm
	Mode register 1 changed, new value is 'mm'.
	Bit meanings, 1/(0):
	b0 = SKIP * not updated here...
	b1 = PARA | LINE | WORD | CHAR
	b2 = WORD | CHAR
	b3 = AUTO | LINE | CHAR

00000100cccccccc
	Special key code, does not generate input directly.
	SKIP, SEARCH, (etc)
	1 = SKIP toggles skl, sets mode1 bit 0 = skl.
	2 = SEARCH toggles indicator/status shl and generates key codes.

000001010000mmmm
	Mode register 2 changed.
	b0 = !ADJUST
	b1 = !SAME (ORG)
	b2 = n.c.
	b3 = n.c.

0000110dtttttttt
	Tape read data, byte 'tt'. Drive 'd' (1=right).
000011100000000d
	Tape read EOF. Drive 'd' (1=right).


The simulator sends the following (binary) codes on it's output pipe:

000001iiiiiiiiii
	Update indicator lamps and illuminated keys.
	Bits are: 0=Record, 1=TapeMovR, 2=TapeMovL, 3=EndDoc, 4=NoAdj,
	5=CharStop, 6=Search, 7=Skip, 8=Code

0000110dtttttttt
	Tape "record" data, byte 'tt'. Drive 'd' (1=right).
000011100000000d
	Tape On for read. Drive 'd' (1=right).
000011100100000d
	Request front-end to send 1 byte from tape. Drive 'd' (1=right).
000011101000000d
	Tape On for write. Drive 'd' (1=right).
000011101100000d
	Tape Off (FE should stop sending, if read). Drive 'd' (1=right).

0001000000rrrrrr
	Print data for "Device 1", Model 601/602/611 "Output Writer".
	'r' is a 6-bit (2+4) "tilt/rotate" code for the typewriter.

000110cccccccccc
	Control command for "Device 1", Model 601/602/611 "Output Writer".
	Codes:	0=Space, 1=BkSpc, 2=Tab, 3=CR/LF, 4=ShiftUp, 5=ShiftDn,
		8=Index, 9=SetTab, 10=ClrTab.

01111111xxxxxxxx
	Reset I/O. 'x' is (should be) ignored.

1111000000000000
	Fatal simulator error. Remaining output until newline is error message.
	At least newline follows.
